      "2026-10-08 owner clarification: three clothing environments only: surface (Seoul cold reference −18.6°C), intermediate underground (8–18°C), and deep underground (18–22°C). Underground is warmer than the surface; no separate shallow tier. Fictional temperatures, not station measurements; no meter boundaries assigned.",
      "2026-10-08 regional scope correction: −18.6°C, 8–18°C, and 18–22°C are Seoul references only. Three environment tiers and occupation-aware clothing apply nationwide; regional temperatures are not assigned from Seoul.",
      "2026-10-08 owner direction: use the 2021-01-08 daily minima of representative stations for all 17 provinces, showing station names and no eup/myeon/dong subdivision. Intermediate/deep underground baselines remain 8–18°C/18–22°C with smaller regional differences; do not propagate surface offsets one-for-one. This supersedes the earlier Seoul-only numeric scope."
    ]
